.TH HD-REBOOT 1 "October 2026" "hd-base" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-reboot, hd-poweroff \- reboot or power off the system, on a desktop and without one
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-reboot
.br
.B hd-poweroff
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-reboot
reboots the system and
.B hd-poweroff
powers it off.
.PP
In a Hyprland session, when hd-desktop is installed, they let its
.I /usr/libexec/hd-desktop/hd-shutdown
close the applications first, which asks with
.BR hd-message (1)
what to do about those that do not close, then runs
.B systemctl reboot
or
.BR "systemctl poweroff" ;
see
.BR hd-desktop (7).
A session is recognized by
.B HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE
in the environment, which Hyprland sets for the programs it starts.
.PP
Otherwise, as on the console, over ssh, or on a system without a desktop,
they run
.B systemctl reboot
or
.B systemctl poweroff
right away.
Whether the user may do that is up to
.BR polkit (8),
as for
.BR systemctl (1)
itself: a user who is logged in on the console of the system may, a user
over ssh is asked for the password of an administrator.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of
.B hd-shutdown
or
.BR systemctl ;
1 when it cannot be started.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-base (7),
.BR hd-desktop (7),
.BR systemctl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
